  "term": "atherosclerosis",
  "definition": "Atherosclerosis is a long-lasting inflammatory disease of the blood vessels. In this condition, stress in the endoplasmic reticulum appears to be an important regulator of vascular injury and is linked with oxidative stress and immune-related processes.",
